    {
     "ruleId": "PRREV-4318-F2-DISPLAY-CHAR-BOUNDARY",
     "level": "warning",
     "message": {
      "text": "F2ValidateReason::BuildIdMismatch's Display slices `&found[..found.len().min(23)]` by BYTE. `found` is the build_id read back from the on-disk F2 receipt JSON (serde, no format check), and the reason is printed by the F2 guard's eprintln at forward_qwen35.rs:1656. A receipt whose build_id has a multi-byte char straddling byte 23 panics the process instead of re-validating. Reproduced with the same expression on \"exe-sha256:x\" + \"é\"*20: rc=101, 'end byte index 23 is not a char boundary'."
     },
     "locations": [
      {
       "physicalLocation": {
        "artifactLocation": {
         "uri": "crates/aprender-serve/src/gguf/inference/forward/f2_receipt.rs"
        },
        "region": {
         "startLine": 170
        }
       }
      }
     ],
     "properties": {
      "grounding": "measured",
      "command": [
       "./slice"
      ],
      "exit_code": 101,
      "stdout_sha256": "a2df3a85e57b2f7f7580ac8340eb29f72dfc1b20126be93b5c11290afb785f39",
      "failure_scenario": "A corrupted or hand-edited F2 receipt with build_id \"exe-sha256:xéé...\" makes every later Qwen3.5 run abort with a slice panic at the F2 decision instead of taking the 'validating on this run' path the mismatch branch exists for; floor to a char boundary (or chars().take(23)).",
      "precision_class": "advisory",
      "rationale_for_class": "Real, measured panic, but reachable only through a non-ASCII build_id in a local receipt file this binary never writes; not a merge block."
     }
    },
    {
     "ruleId": "PRREV-4318-DUP-FILE-SHA256",
     "level": "note",
     "message": {
      "text": "The diff adds `pub fn file_sha256(path) -> io::Result<String>` (streamed sha256, lower-hex) in aprender-serve f2_receipt.rs:400. The duplication scan hit a pre-existing same-name, same-purpose `fn file_sha256(path) -> Option<String>` at crates/apr-cli/src/commands/bench.rs:309 (PARITY-001); apr-cli already depends on aprender-serve, so bench.rs could reuse the new public one."
     },
     "locations": [
      {
